# Tests that tests/run.sh --target linux-arm64 does not build: "dir/name reason".

run/when_top a when TARGET_ARCH == X86_64 with no other branch: the program is written for x86-64 only
fail/when_order the error it expects comes from the branch of when TARGET_ARCH == X86_64, which arm64 does not take
sys/backtrace_c_callback calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/backtrace_c_fault calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/c_variadic calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/thread_ccb calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/thread_ccb_panic calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/thread_libc calls the C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
run/debug_info -g: debug information is not written for linux-arm64 yet (refused with a message)
std/input reads gamepads with x86-64 system call numbers (std.input_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/input_gamepad_watch reads gamepads with x86-64 system call numbers (std.input_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/net_dns std.net uses x86-64 system call numbers (std.net_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/net_http std.net uses x86-64 system call numbers (std.net_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/net_ipv6 std.net uses x86-64 system call numbers (std.net_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/net_tcp std.net uses x86-64 system call numbers (std.net_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/net_udp std.net uses x86-64 system call numbers (std.net_linux): refused for linux-arm64
std/window_wayland_logic the Wayland helpers of std.window live in std.window_wayland, which makes x86-64 system calls (memfd, mmap, poll): refused for linux-arm64
